<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <%# Per-page title, derived from the last breadcrumb - the one without a path,
        which every admin controller already sets to the current page's label. Was
        a single static string on every admin page (WCAG 2.4.2), still using the
        old un-spaced brand name. %>
    <% admin_page_title = @breadcrumbs&.last&.dig(:label).presence || "Admin" %>
    <title><%= admin_page_title %> | Admin | Stocks in the Future</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :app, 'data-turbo-track': "reload" %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "actiontext", 'data-turbo-track': "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-slate-50" data-controller="drawer table-scroll">
    <%# Admin Header %>
    <%= render "layouts/environment_ribbon" %>

    <div class="fixed <%= header_top_class %> left-0 w-full z-50 bg-white border-b border-slate-200">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between py-3 px-4 h-16 lg:px-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
          <%# A button, not a label driving a hidden checkbox, and it reports its own state. %>
          <button type="button"
                  data-drawer-target="trigger"
                  data-action="drawer#toggle"
                  data-testid="open-navigation"
                  aria-expanded="false"
                  aria-controls="admin-navigation"
                  class="lg:hidden inline-flex min-h-11 min-w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-slate-600 transition-colors hover:bg-slate-100 hover:text-slate-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary">
            <span class="sr-only">Open navigation menu</span>
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h16" />
            </svg>
          </button>
<%# Branding and a link home, not a page heading. This was an h1, so every
    admin page announced the same title regardless of what it showed, and
    /admin ended up with three. The real heading is in the content area. %>
<span class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
            <%= link_to admin_root_path, class: "inline-flex items-center rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary" do %>
              <%= lucide_icon("wrench", class: "text-sitf-primary mr-2 w-4 h-4 shrink-0") %>
              Admin
            <% end %>
          </span>
        </div>
        <%# Was the email as plain text plus two bare links, one of them "Sign out" in
            red-600 on white - 4.0:1, under the gate. Same account menu as the main app, so
            there is one place to see who is signed in and one way to leave. %>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1">
          <%# The way back to the student-facing app. It was an item inside the account menu, which
              is wrong twice over: it is a destination rather than an account action, and a
              destination behind an avatar is not discoverable - which was the report.

              It lives in the top bar because that is where WordPress ("Visit Site") and Django
              ("VIEW SITE") both put it, and because the sidebar has no room: a footer row there
              pushed the admin nav 68px past a 1366x768 Chromebook, which spacing_test caught. The
              label is hidden below lg, where the bar holds a trigger, a wordmark and an avatar
              already - the icon and its accessible name carry it there. %>
          <%= link_to root_path, class: ghost_class, title: "View site" do %>
            <%= lucide_icon("house", class: "size-4 shrink-0") %>
            <span class="hidden lg:inline">View site</span>
            <span class="sr-only lg:hidden">View site</span>
          <% end %>

          <%= render 'layouts/account_menu' %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# One nav element that translates, rather than a desktop copy plus a mobile copy of the
        same markup. The scrim toggles a single `hidden` class - it used to toggle that class
        *and* an inline display style, which fought each other. %>
    <div class="fixed inset-0 z-40 hidden bg-black/50 lg:hidden"
         data-drawer-target="scrim"
         data-action="click->drawer#close"
         aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <nav id="admin-navigation"
         aria-label="Admin"
         data-drawer-target="panel"
         data-action="click->drawer#closeIfLink"
         class="fixed <%= drawer_top_class %> left-0 z-50 <%= drawer_height_class %> w-64 -translate-x-full transform overflow-y-auto border-r border-slate-200 bg-white transition-transform duration-300 lg:translate-x-0">
      <div class="p-4">
        <%# Mobile only: at lg the sidebar is permanent, so there is nothing to close. %>
        <button type="button"
                data-action="drawer#close"
                data-testid="close-navigation"
                class="lg:hidden mb-2 ml-auto flex min-h-11 min-w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-slate-700 transition-colors hover:bg-slate-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary">
          <span class="sr-only">Close navigation menu</span>
          <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12" />
          </svg>
        </button>

        <%= render "admin/shared/navigation" %>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <%# Main Content %>
    <main class="<%= main_offset_class(:padding) %> lg:pl-64 min-h-screen">
      <div class="p-4 lg:p-6">
        <%# The content column, around the flash and the page both, exactly as the app layout does
            it. Admin had the same split: every admin page wraps itself in `max-w-7xl mx-auto` while
            the flash was a bare child of this wrapper, so at 1920px a flash measured 1616px against
            content of 1280px. One product, one rule - a fix on the app side alone would have left
            admin as the only half where a banner is wider than the page. %>
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
          <%# The shared partial, so admin gets the same role=status announcement and
              the icon-plus-text treatment as the rest of the app. %>
          <%= render "layouts/flash" %>

          <%# The page heading, from the same breadcrumb the title uses. Admin pages
              previously had no heading describing them - their only h1 was the
              branding in the header bar, identical on every page.

              Index and show pages lead with a section title rather than a page
              title, so this is visually hidden to avoid saying the same word twice
              on screen while still naming the page for assistive tech. A page that
              has its own visible h1 declares `content_for :own_heading` and this
              steps aside. %>
          <% unless content_for?(:own_heading) %>
            <h1 class="sr-only"><%= @breadcrumbs&.last&.dig(:label).presence || "Admin dashboard" %></h1>
          <% end %>

          <%= yield %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <%# One product, one confirmation dialog. Admin carries most of the destructive actions in the app. %>
    <%= render "shared/confirm_dialog" %>
  </body>
</html>
